; ======================================================================
;  hw_bt_payload.pi4 - the HwBt* seam (Anvil/Hal/hal.pbi) for a RAM
;  PAYLOAD on the Pi 4 that runs Anvil's Bluetooth stack itself
;  (Anvil/Net/hci.pbi, l2cap.pbi, a2dp.pbi) - the NES payload, the
;  pi4BtProbe diagnostic. A payload owns the machine while it runs, so
;  there is no console to lend: bt_uart.pi4 borrows the PL011 and gives
;  every register back at HwBtClose (BtuClose).
;
;  The monitor's own seam is RaspberryPi4/Board/hw_bt.pi4 (it also tells
;  uart.pi4 the PL011 is lent). Include ONE of the two, after
;  RaspberryPi4/Lib/bt_uart.pi4 and before Anvil/Net/hci.pbi.
;  Pi 4 (BCM2711) only.
; ======================================================================

Procedure.i HwBtOpen()
  BtuMayBorrowConsole(1)
  ProcedureReturn BtuOpen()
EndProcedure

Procedure HwBtClose()
  BtuClose()
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwBtPut(b.i)
  ProcedureReturn BtuPut(b)
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwBtGet()
  ProcedureReturn BtuGet()
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwBtSetBaud(baud.i)
  ProcedureReturn BtuSetBaud(baud)
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwBtWhy()
  ProcedureReturn BtuWhy()
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwBtConsoleLent()
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure
